--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,26 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Sign-up phone verification
+
+Set `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, and `TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER` on the
+server (see `.env.example`). For local development, copy these values into `.env`.
+The sender must be an SMS-capable Twilio number. Without credentials the form
+reports that SMS verification is unavailable; it never simulates verification.
+
+Sign-up sends an origin-bound SMS with `@hostname #code` on the final line.
+Use HTTPS in production for WebOTP. Browsers without WebOTP can use keyboard
+SMS autofill or enter/paste the six-digit code. Codes expire after five minutes,
+allow five incorrect attempts, and can be resent after 60 seconds. Resending
+replaces the old code. Registration is sent to the existing account service only
+after the server validates the code against the phone and browser session.
+
+Astro's Node adapter stores sessions on disk by default. For multiple instances,
+configure shared session storage and a shared SMS rate limiter; the additional
+phone resend limiter here runs within one server process. The external account
+service must also enforce phone verification if direct registrations to that
+service need to be prohibited; this repository only controls its own sign-up route.
+
+Run `node --test tests/signup.test.ts` to check the verification route without
+sending SMS messages or creating real accounts.
